# Content contracts

Read `docs/content-contracts.md` before creating or changing reader-facing
historical content. Start from the matching file in `templates/season/` or
`templates/race/`; shared schemas live in `templates/shared/`.

- Choose exactly one document type and its associated knowledge boundary.
- Declare every required field from `docs/temporal-scope.md` in the document's
  sibling `.meta.yaml` (Markdown has no YAML front matter).
- Keep allowed and forbidden knowledge, sections, source expectations, length,
  primary-home boundaries, and audits consistent with that contract.
- Season-teams entries must cover organisation, personnel, and sponsors (or
  explicit uncertainty), not only drivers and equipment; see the Season teams
  checklist in `docs/content-contracts.md`.
- Do not advance workflow status until source and spoiler audits pass.
- Never mutate an earlier-boundary document to include a later state; create the
  separately contracted document only when explicitly tasked.

The `archive/**/*.md` scope does not authorise historical content. Creating a
real season or race directory still requires an explicit task.
